<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sabium</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1844–1831 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century-bce">19th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sabium was an early king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-babylonian-empire">First Dynasty of Babylon</a> in the nineteenth century BCE. He was one of the five rulers, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumuabum">Sumuabum</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sin-muballit">Sin-muballit</a>, who preceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a>. Accounts of the Babylonian Empire describe these kings as having slowly built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> from a minor city-state into a recognised regional power by completing its walls and developing its infrastructure.</p></div>
